1
00:00:06,418 --> 00:00:09,110
The dress is seen as white and gold.

2
00:00:09,190 --> 00:00:11,547
Or it is seen as blue and black.

3
00:00:12,374 --> 00:00:15,664
The same lines are seen
as a duck, or as a rabbit.

4
00:00:15,744 --> 00:00:18,952
The same electron appears
as a particle or a wave,

5
00:00:19,032 --> 00:00:20,868
depending on how it is asked.

6
00:00:20,948 --> 00:00:26,402
If nothing is fixed from its own side,
appearances seem endlessly malleable.

7
00:00:27,234 --> 00:00:29,872
So a subtler idea suggests itself.

8
00:00:29,952 --> 00:00:33,581
Perhaps there is a store of
potentials behind appearances,

9
00:00:33,661 --> 00:00:37,562
from which they are drawn.
Aristotle spoke of potency.

10
00:00:37,642 --> 00:00:39,994
Heisenberg spoke of potentia.

11
00:00:40,074 --> 00:00:44,247
Quantum theory describes an
abstract space of possibilities.

12
00:00:44,327 --> 00:00:47,820
On this picture, appearances
are what gets actualised.

13
00:00:47,900 --> 00:00:50,134
The potentials are what is really there.

14
00:00:50,937 --> 00:00:54,009
In this book's reading,
that makes a substrate,

15
00:00:54,089 --> 00:00:56,590
a hidden base, for emptiness.

16
00:00:56,670 --> 00:01:01,319
Emptiness here means the absence of any
nature a thing would have from its own

17
00:01:01,399 --> 00:01:05,626
side. The mind sees that
phenomena have no fixed nature.

18
00:01:05,706 --> 00:01:08,384
Then it gives their
openness a home behind them.

19
00:01:08,464 --> 00:01:13,579
Emptiness becomes a new substance,
made of possibilities instead of stuff.

20
00:01:14,402 --> 00:01:19,282
But a potential is known only through
what it becomes, and through its partner.

21
00:01:19,362 --> 00:01:22,515
Salt is soluble only in relation to water.

22
00:01:22,595 --> 00:01:26,052
A seed is a seed only in
relation to the sprout.

23
00:01:26,182 --> 00:01:28,969
"Could" is said within
a set of conditions.

24
00:01:29,049 --> 00:01:31,306
It is not a thing waiting backstage.

25
00:01:31,386 --> 00:01:35,246
When Nāgārjuna says that for
whom emptiness is possible,

26
00:01:35,326 --> 00:01:39,893
everything is possible, the
word means "fits", or "works".

27
00:01:39,973 --> 00:01:42,031
It does not describe a reservoir.

28
00:01:42,833 --> 00:01:44,899
Nor is the openness endless.

29
00:01:44,979 --> 00:01:47,399
Appearances are open because they depend.

30
00:01:47,479 --> 00:01:49,533
They are limited for the same reason.

31
00:01:49,613 --> 00:01:52,399
A rope can appear as a snake in dim light.

32
00:01:52,479 --> 00:01:55,511
A shadow cannot be walked
across as a bridge.

33
00:01:55,591 --> 00:01:58,541
The dress split its viewers
into two colourings,

34
00:01:58,621 --> 00:02:01,032
not into every colour at once.

35
00:02:01,845 --> 00:02:06,688
A plasticity free of all conditions
would be its own kind of own-nature:

36
00:02:06,790 --> 00:02:10,460
a power able to make
anything, from its own side.

37
00:02:10,540 --> 00:02:13,735
That is the idealist
extreme, not the Middle Way.

38
00:02:13,815 --> 00:02:18,834
Appearances are exactly as plastic as
their conditions allow, and no more.

39
00:02:19,633 --> 00:02:22,243
Dzogchen has a better word than potential:

40
00:02:22,323 --> 00:02:24,761
ma 'gags pa, unobstructed.

41
00:02:25,565 --> 00:02:27,237
Nothing blocks the display.

42
00:02:27,317 --> 00:02:31,196
And there is no store behind it,
from which the display comes.

